  "report_markdown": "## Executive Summary\n\n- In 2004, EA bought Criterion, the studio behind Burnout.\n- Criterion also built RenderWare, tech that ran a huge chunk of the games industry at the time.\n- Radical Entertainment existed from 1991 to 2012.\n- Guerrilla Cambridge existed from 1989 to 2017.\n- Silicon Knights existed from 1992 to 2014.\n- Acclaim Entertainment existed from 1987 to 2004.\n- Zipper Interactive existed from 1995 to 2012.\n- Bizarre Creations existed from 1988 to 2011.\n- Psygnosis/Sony Liverpool existed from 1984 to 2012.\n- Lionhead Studios existed from 1997 to 2016.\n- Free Radical Design existed from 1998 to 2014.\n- Ensemble Studios existed from 1995 to 2009.\n- Pandemic existed from 1998 to 2009.\n- Clover Studios existed from 2004 to 2007.\n- Visceral Games existed from 1998 to 2017.\n- Neversoft existed from 1994 to 2014.\n- Grand Theft Auto is a 1997 action-adventure game developed by DMA Design and published by BMG Interactive.\n- Grand Theft Auto is the first game in the Grand Theft Auto series and was released in November 1997 for MS-DOS and Windows, in December 1997 for the PlayStation and in October 1999 for the Game Boy Color.\n- The Grand Theft Auto gameplay is presented from a top-down perspective.\n- LOST IN TIME is a time travel card game for 1 to 4 players ages 10 and up.\n- LOST IN TIME is a time travel card game that was the first English review of the game.\n- LOST IN TIME was an introductory game to a 3 part series on the theme of time travel.\n",
